Andy Wilson responded to my challenge to name "PLENTY of ways" to
incapacitate attackers--such as the BATF in Waco--without the use
of deadly force:

    "I mean PLENTY in terms of possibilities,  although I
    realize that there aren't very many realistic
    alternatives to guns at this point."

BINGO, except that there aren't ANY realistic alternatives to
guns (see below).

    ". . . (1) a large portion of fatal shootings occur
    within households.  (2) And around half of all police
    officers killed by guns are killed with their OWN guns.
    (3) It would be difficult to kill an police officer with
    their own gun in England, since they don't carry them."

(1) This is a variation on a classic myth promulgated by the gun
grabbers.  Once you factor out suicide, "righteous" shoots and
killings among criminal associates, there isn't much left.  For
hard, academically rigorous treatment of the subject, read
anything by Prof. Don Kates.  I especially recommend RESTRICTING
HANDGUNS: THE LIBERAL SCEPTICS SPEAK OUT.

(2) True, but irrelevant.  The alternative is to be killed by
someone else's gun, knife, club or boot.

(3) Violence against cops in England is on the rise.  To offset
this trend, more and more often, police ARE being armed with guns
in England.  Why?  It works.

Andy than suggested several alternatives to guns:

    "- chemicals (mace, tear gas, etc)"

Not even close.  When I went through a mace course taught by a
police officer, he gave us this advice:  "Don't ever use mace on
a cop.  He'll pull out his gun and shoot you."  (If you still
believe [non-lethal] chemicals will do the trick, I have an
interesting wager to propose to you.)

    "- tranquilizer darts"

Spare me.  These represent the worst of all possible worlds.
They do NOTHING in the short term, but can be FATAL in the long
term.  Shoot your attacker with one and he will beat your brains
out, long before he goes sleepy-by.  He might go into shock and
die later, but you will have long since assumed room temperature.

    "- tasers"

Nope.  None of the electrical stuff works worth a damn.  Tasers
didn't stop Rodney King and they won't stop you if you are
wearing a leather jacket or even a thick sweater.  Stun guns look
pretty, but are next to useless.  I used to work in a "spy store"
that sold stun guns.  We regularly tested them on a guy who used
to come by the shop.  He was a telephone "psychic" who had been
struck by lightening . . . twice.  He could take everything we
gave him.  I accidentally zapped myself once with 80k volts (low
amperage).  It SMARTED.  Again, I have a wager for you if you
still think this junk is a real self-defense contender.

    "- low-frequency sound waves"

Uh-huh.  Right.  I'm not sure WHAT this means.  I guess when the
BATF comes to Tim's house he should sing "Ol' Man River" basso
profundo?

    "- things that haven't been invented yet"

Hey Andy, ya' got me there!  "Landing party, the Batfs are
approaching, set your phasers to stun."

Finally, Andy wrote:

    "Also, I'm sure the government has developed some things
    along these lines [non-lethal self-defense] in
    classified research projects."

Why?  Guns, tanks and bombs achieve the government's end quite
well.  All of this talk about substituting fanciful chimeras for
guns is nothing more than *WISHFUL THINKING*.  Unfortunately,
wishing does not make it so.  Wake up and smell the cordite.

